  "description": "EZIFEB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C106 H110 Gd8 N30 O46,6(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.514-3.834 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.73-111.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C112H134Gd8N30O52.",
